      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is not that easy - I need to add `tpmh-\u003ecommand_code` as a parameter to `extension_route_command()` to differentiate Strongbox commands from other vendor commands and define flag:\n```\nbool is_strongbox \u003d (tpm_command_code \u003d\u003d (TPM_CC_VENDOR_STRONGBOX |\n\t\t\t\t\tTPM_CC_VENDOR_BIT_MASK));\n```\n\nJust using `p-\u003ecode` doesn\u0027t work due to overlap of subcommand codes. The end result is that it is not clear if we save something, but we clutter logic adding `!is_strongbox` to conditions. As for different interfaces it seems that it is easier to add this simple check in a new function than to add more checks into `extension_route_command()`.\n\nInstead, I just added potential logic into `extension_route_strongbox_command()`.",
